# Jaguar Mark 1 3.4 Litre four-door saloon, 1957-1959.
#
# The 3.4-litre version of the compact Mark 1: the same shell as the 2.4 with
# the larger engine, a different grille and lamp treatment and, from 1957, disc
# brakes. It was replaced by the Mark 2 in 1959.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_Mark_1
#
# Dimensions 4.60 x 1.70 x 1.45 m, wheelbase 2.73 m.
#
# Shape reference: no side, no rear and no badge close-up exist in the pack.
# The best images are front three-quarters about 40 degrees off and a dead-on
# front. The flank and tail are reconciled within the published dimensions, and
# the 3.4 identification rests on the uploaders' titles because no boot badge is
# legible. Both limitations are recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no UK brochure was consulted. British Racing Green,
# Black, Pearl Grey and Carmen Red are period Jaguar finishes. Weights 4, 3, 2,
# 1, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 180 km/h. Comfort 75/443, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 75. Classes 3,4.
# Dates 1957-1959 production, road tail staggered 1972-1974.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-mk1-34.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaguar-mk1-34.dae. References:
# citycars/references/jaguar-mk1-34/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: built as a variant of the Mark 1 2.4 master. No side, no
# rear and no badge close-up exist in the pack; the 3.4 identification rests on
# the uploaders' titles, and the flank and tail are reconciled within the
# published dimensions.


